## Part 8: KEY PRINCIPLES TO FOLLOW

### ✅ DO THIS:
- ✅ One file = one responsibility
- ✅ Clear function names: `validate_smiles()`, not `check()`
- ✅ Docstrings on every function explaining what it does, inputs, outputs
- ✅ Handle errors gracefully (try/except, informative messages)
- ✅ Log progress (print what's happening, so user knows it's working)
- ✅ Use modern RDKit API (2025.x compatible)
- ✅ Test edge cases ("BANANA", empty input, etc.)
- ✅ Save intermediate results (model, metrics, metadata)
- ✅ Document why, not just what

### ❌ DON'T DO THIS:
- ❌ Mix concerns (don't put data loading + model training in same file)
- ❌ Use vague variable names (`x`, `data`, `result`)
- ❌ Silently fail (always tell user what went wrong)
- ❌ Assume perfect input (validate everything)
- ❌ List comprehensions for 10^9 items (use parallelization)
- ❌ Call it "QSAR" (it's not—be precise with terminology)
- ❌ Report only sigma (report MAE, RMSE, R²)
- ❌ Redundant type casts
- ❌ Monolithic files

